  - [1mA. Quick views plus a week picker:[0m three radio buttons (All events, Failed sign-ins, Security changes) and a week
    dropdown. Each of your cases is one click, and it's the smallest diff. You can't filter to a single type like
    "Password changed." Adding that later means swapping in a different control, which is a small, contained change.
  - [1mB. Checkbox list of all nine types plus a week picker:[0m any mix of types. Security changes takes four clicks, and the
    list takes up a lot of room on a phone (the guidelines require the page to work at 320px wide).
  - [1mC. Quick views that fill in the checkbox list:[0m one-click views plus fine-tuning. This is the most code and the most
    to review, and preset buttons that change a checkbox list aren't covered by the component specs.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. It matches the three things you said people need. The guidelines call for a radio group when there are
  2 to 5 options, so it needs no new component. It also keeps the diff small.

  Pick one in the browser or reply here. Which events count as "security changes" is the next question.

